# Node: atomic.ByBuiltinRule.InFact.PowerSetMembership
# Run: target/release/litex -strict -f examples/proof_nodes/atomic/by_builtin_rule/in_power_set_from_restricted_image.lit
# Before: by-def proved the subset; the following same membership failed search
# after parent WD succeeded, because its subset premise repeated WD below it.
# fn_range(fn(point K) Y {f(point)}) $in power_set(Y)
# After: the known-subset route preserves its real citation and parent objects' WD.

claim:
    ? forall X, Y set, f fn(arg X) Y, K power_set(X):
        fn_range(fn(point K) Y {f(point)}) $in power_set(Y)
    by def:
        ? fn_range(fn(point K) Y {f(point)}) $subset Y
    fn_range(fn(point K) Y {f(point)}) $in power_set(Y)
